ION 1.6.0 r22909 : flyingcomponents - This property determines whether the detached components such as doors, bumpers, etc., should respawn after a vehicle is recreated (change model or variant) or streamed in. (default: true) ADDED/UPDATED IN VERSION 1.6.0 r23223 : vehicleburnexplosions - This property toggles creation of additional explosions ( type 2 - rocket ) when plane or helicopter is burning. (default: true) ADDED/UPDATED IN VERSION 1.6.0 r23237 : vehicle_engine_autostart - This property toggles automatic vehicle engine state behavior. (default: true) If you set it to false then vehicle engine will not start on driver enter and will not stop on driver exit. To control the engine you need to use setVehicleEngineState . Helicopter rotors will spin only if the engine is on (with or without driver inside). This flag also affects bikes
